{"query_id": "dp-long-chronicle", "tags": ["long-document"], "dimensions": ["long-document"], "answer": "The Mill Lane chronicle records the following events regarding Greassby Mill:\n\n*   In 1850-11-18, the wheel at Greassby Mill turned again for the first time since the flood, watched by most of the street [5].\n*   On 1860-02-24, Greassby Mill was sold by the estate to the miller's family, and the deed was witnessed at the inn [15].\n*   Greassby Mill stood idle for 44 weeks while the millstones were re-dressed by a man brought in from the next county [19].\n*   On 1887-12-21, the last miller at Greassby Mill retired, and the building was let as a store [18].\n*   The parish raised £4,525.32 by subscription to repair the roof of Greassby Mill after the gale [20].\n*   After the weir upstream was lowered, the leat at Greassby Mill carried only 17.5 per cent of its old flow [21].", "answer_sha256": "42cb41166b3428bb0afd2d004bc6851933a5d14dc3bb1b7d20d390cfabd46795", "ranked_ids": ["chronicle-long"], "citation_map": {"1": "chronicle-long", "10": "chronicle-long", "11": "chronicle-long", "12": "chronicle-long", "13": "chronicle-long", "14": "chronicle-long", "15": "chronicle-long", "16": "chronicle-long", "17": "chronicle-long", "18": "chronicle-long", "19": "chronicle-long", "2": "chronicle-long", "20": "chronicle-long", "21": "chronicle-long", "22": "chronicle-long", "23": "chronicle-long", "24": "chronicle-long", "25": "chronicle-long", "26": "chronicle-long", "27": "chronicle-long", "28": "chronicle-long", "3": "chronicle-long", "4": "chronicle-long", "5": "chronicle-long", "6": "chronicle-long", "7": "chronicle-long", "8": "chronicle-long", "9": "chronicle-long"}, "cited_ids": [5, 15, 19, 18, 20, 21], "cited_document_ids": ["chronicle-long"], "invalid_citations": [], "abstained": false, "expected_abstain": false, "mechanical_checks_passed": true, "answer_correct": null, "review_status": "unreviewed", "latency_ms": 105689, "model": "Qwen3.5-9B-Q4_K_M.gguf", "erro